         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/british-columbia/ai-data-centre-telus-vancouver-9.7424536?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/dc1b8076-8041-4d73-a680-dea1263ca1b0,1794922863904/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C265%2C3000%2C1687%29%3B' alt='A large metal facility is shown with a sports stadium in the background.' width='620' height='349' title='A rendering of a proposed Telus data centre near B.C. Place in downtown Vancouver.'/><p>Telus says it's decided not to proceed with co-developing two Vancouver data centres, and will instead turn its focus to expanding an existing data centre in Kamloops, B.C.</p>]]></description>
